      "id": "claim_0f9bef07360b4e6e81200303d9e46e00",
      "statement": "DiskManager::defragment_safe implements a 6-step safe compaction workflow: copy image to temp, collect inodes (preserving directory blocks), clear+rewrite data bitmap preserving directory blocks, sequentially reallocate file payloads contiguously, flush, then atomically replace the image via a 3-step rename with rollback from .old on any failure.",
